### Meters & Meter Readings — Homebase API
### Base URL: http://localhost:3000

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
@unitId = 0192f58e-4a61-7bf0-8e6f-47dc2e0f49f6
@propertyId = 0192f58e-4a61-7bf0-8e6f-47dc2e0f49f5
@meterId = 0192f58e-4a61-7bf0-8e6f-47dc2e0f49f8

### 1. Create a Water Meter
POST {{baseUrl}}/meters
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "unitId": "{{unitId}}",
  "meterType": "WATER",
  "meterNumber": "WM-001",
  "lastReading": 1200,
  "pricePerUnit": 150.00
}

### 2. Create an Electricity Meter
POST {{baseUrl}}/meters
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "unitId": "{{unitId}}",
  "meterType": "ELECTRICITY",
  "meterNumber": "EM-001",
  "lastReading": 500,
  "pricePerUnit": 35.50
}

### 3. Get All Meters (with Pagination)
GET {{baseUrl}}/meters?page=1&limit=10

### 4. Get Meters Filtered by Unit
GET {{baseUrl}}/meters?unitId={{unitId}}

### 5. Get Meters Filtered by Property
GET {{baseUrl}}/meters?propertyId={{propertyId}}

### 6. Get Meters Filtered by Type
GET {{baseUrl}}/meters?meterType=WATER

### 7. Get Meter Details (with latest readings)
GET {{baseUrl}}/meters/{{meterId}}

### 8. Update a Meter (e.g. price or meter number)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/meters/{{meterId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "pricePerUnit": 160.00,
  "meterNumber": "WM-001-RENAMED"
}

### 9. Record a Reading (computes unitsConsumed & consumptionCost)
POST {{baseUrl}}/meters/{{meterId}}/readings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "currentReading": 1350
}

### 10. Record a Reading with a Custom Date
POST {{baseUrl}}/meters/{{meterId}}/readings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "currentReading": 1500,
  "readingDate": "2026-10-01T00:00:00.000Z"
}

### 11. Get Reading History for a Meter (Paginated)
GET {{baseUrl}}/meters/{{meterId}}/readings?page=1&limit=10

### 12. Delete a Meter
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/meters/{{meterId}}